Good news — there's already a detailed setup guide in the project. But I notice the setup guide references port 3000, and since I changed the default port to 5000 for Replit, I should fix that. Let me update the guide to be accurate:

The project actually already includes a full setup guide (VSCODE_SETUP.md) in the file explorer. Here's the short version of what you need to do:

1. Install Node.js (if you haven't already)
Download the LTS version from nodejs.org

2. Get the code on your machine
Clone or download this repo to somewhere permanent, like:

Windows: C:\Tools\local-agent
Mac/Linux: ~/tools/local-agent
3. Install dependencies (one time)
Open a terminal in that folder and run:

npm install
4. Add your OpenAI API key
Copy .env.example to .env, then open .env and fill in your actual key:

OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...your key here...
5. Run it against your project
The recommended approach is to open your project folder in VS Code, open the terminal, and point it at the agent:

node C:\Tools\local-agent\server.js   (Windows)
node ~/tools/local-agent/server.js    (Mac/Linux)
Then open http://localhost:5000 in your browser. The agent will operate on whatever folder you launched from.

Tip: The setup guide also covers optional shortcuts — like a one-click VS Code task and shell scripts — so you don't have to type the full path every time. It's worth a read once you're set up.
